# The image must not depend on where it was built.
#
# `COPY . .` obeys this file, not .gitignore. Without it a local build bakes in whatever
# happens to be on that machine — 40MB of generated snapshots, 48MB of past results, a 97MB
# .git, the beads Dolt database — while a CI build (which checks out from git) does not. Same
# Dockerfile, two different images, and the manifest could not tell them apart.
#
# Snapshots stay out deliberately: they are regenerated on the instance from a fixed seed
# (GENERATE_MISSING=1 reproduces the committed checksums exactly) or seeded over the wire.
outputs/
results/
figures/
.git/
.github/
.beads/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
py312/
.env
*.log
*.duckdb
*.parquet
rust-harness/target/
bench/*/target/
